#!/bin/bash

# ============================================================================
# OBSOLETE: This script is for Linux builds and is NO LONGER USED
# ============================================================================

cat << 'EOF'
============================================================================
OBSOLETE SCRIPT - USE ZEPHYR BUILD SYSTEM
============================================================================

This script was designed for Linux compilation and is no longer used.
This project has been converted to use Zephyr RTOS build system.

NEW BUILD PROCESS:
==================

1. Build the Zephyr application:
   ./build_zephyr.sh

2. Run on Spike simulator:
   ./run_spike.sh

3. Or use west directly:
   west build -p -b spike_riscv64 .
   spike -p4 --isa=rv64gcv_zicntr build/zephyr/zephyr.elf

WHY THE CHANGE:
===============

- Proper integration with Zephyr RTOS kernel
- Correct memory management (k_aligned_alloc/k_free)
- Proper timing subsystem integration
- Console output via printk()
- Better resource management and error handling
- Designed for embedded/RTOS environment

FILES:
======

- CMakeLists.txt     : Zephyr build configuration
- prj.conf           : Project configuration  
- src/main.cpp       : Zephyr application entry point
- build_zephyr.sh    : Build script
- run_spike.sh       : Spike execution script
- README_Zephyr.md   : Complete documentation

ENVIRONMENT SETUP:
==================

export ZEPHYR_BASE=$(pwd)  # from zephyr root directory
export ZEPHYR_TOOLCHAIN_VARIANT=cross-compile
export CROSS_COMPILE=/path/to/riscv64-unknown-elf-

See README_Zephyr.md for complete instructions.

============================================================================
EOF